# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box, 216-atom box): the engine agrees with native to 5.7e-13 relative in every thermo value and to 2.5e-12 per atom (force and position); 1e-10 is the tightest tolerance measured on these cases.
# oracle: the AMOEBA water box of examples/amoeba as in w119amoeba_full_box, cut to its first 72 molecules (w119amoeba_box_k72.data: 216 atoms instead of 648, the 648-atom run took 21 s; the molecules keep the box size, so the density is a third of the example's, ewald, pme-grid 24, cutoff 7 taper 6, polar-eps 1e-5), with 10 NVE steps (fix nve, dt 1 fs in real units) after the step-0 state; thermo every 5 steps and the atom forces and positions at step 10 are compared.
# oracle-inputs: w119amoeba_box_k72.data w119amoeba_water.prm w119amoeba_box_full.key
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 abs=1e-10
units           real
boundary        p p p
atom_style      amoeba
bond_style      class2
angle_style     amoeba
dihedral_style  none
fix             amtype all property/atom i_amtype ghost yes
fix             extra all property/atom i_amgroup d_redID d_pval ghost yes
fix             extra2 all property/atom i_polaxe d2_xyzaxis 3
read_data       w119amoeba_box_k72.data fix amtype NULL "Tinker Types"
special_bonds   lj/coul 0.5 0.5 0.5 one/five yes
pair_style      amoeba
pair_coeff      * * w119amoeba_water.prm w119amoeba_box_full.key
compute         p all pair amoeba
compute         virial all pressure NULL virial
fix             nve all nve
timestep        1.0
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl c_p[1] c_p[2] c_p[3] c_p[4] c_p[5] c_p[6] press c_virial[1] c_virial[2] c_virial[3] c_virial[4] c_virial[5] c_virial[6]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             10
